  "comments": {
   "FUNCTION": [
    "An ATP-dependent 3'-5' DNA helicase, loads on a 3'-tailed substrate and unwinds DNA as it translocates in a 3'-5' direction (PubMed:22641846). The (d)ATPase activity is dependent on single-stranded (ss)DNA, only (d)ATP allows helicase activity; no other nucleotides are hydrolyzed (PubMed:22641846). Has no activity on 5'-tailed or blunt-ended DNA (PubMed:22641846)"
   ],
   "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY": [
    "Couples ATP hydrolysis with the unwinding of duplex DNA by translocating in the 3'-5' direction.",
    "ATP + H2O = ADP + phosphate + H(+)"
   ],
   "COFACTOR": [
    "a divalent metal cation",
    "Zn(2+)"
   ],
   "SUBUNIT": [
    "Monomer"
   ],
   "DOMAIN": [
    "The C-terminus is required for production of properly folded protein; deletion of the last 75 residues makes an insoluble protein in E.coli"
   ],
   "SIMILARITY": [
    "Belongs to the helicase family. HRQ1 subfamily"
   ]
